  30:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****     [..]
  31:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****       (#) Initialize the CAN low level resources by implementing the
  32:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****           HAL_CAN_MspInit():
  33:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****          (++) Enable the CAN interface clock using __HAL_RCC_CANx_CLK_ENABLE()
  34:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****          (++) Configure CAN pins
  35:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****              (+++) Enable the clock for the CAN GPIOs
  36:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****              (+++) Configure CAN pins as alternate function
  37:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****          (++) In case of using interrupts (e.g. HAL_CAN_ActivateNotification())
  38:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****              (+++) Configure the CAN interrupt priority using
  39:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****                    HAL_NVIC_SetPriority()
  40:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****              (+++) Enable the CAN IRQ handler using HAL_NVIC_EnableIRQ()
  41:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****              (+++) In CAN IRQ handler, call HAL_CAN_IRQHandler()
  42:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c **** 
  43:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****       (#) Initialize the CAN peripheral using HAL_CAN_Init() function. This
  44:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****           function resorts to HAL_CAN_MspInit() for low-level initialization.
  45:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c **** 
  46:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****       (#) Configure the reception filters using the following configuration
  47:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****           functions:
  48:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****             (++) HAL_CAN_ConfigFilter()
  49:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c **** 
  50:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****       (#) Start the CAN module using HAL_CAN_Start() function. At this level
  51:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****           the node is active on the bus: it receive messages, and can send
  52:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****           messages.
  53:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c **** 
  54:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****       (#) To manage messages transmission, the following Tx control functions
  55:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****           can be used:
  56:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****             (++) HAL_CAN_AddTxMessage() to request transmission of a new
  57:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****                  message.
  58:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****             (++) HAL_CAN_AbortTxRequest() to abort transmission of a pending
  59:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****                  message.
  60:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****             (++) HAL_CAN_GetTxMailboxesFreeLevel() to get the number of free Tx
  61:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****                  mailboxes.
  62:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****             (++) HAL_CAN_IsTxMessagePending() to check if a message is pending
  63:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****                  in a Tx mailbox.
  64:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****             (++) HAL_CAN_GetTxTimestamp() to get the timestamp of Tx message
  65:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****                  sent, if time triggered communication mode is enabled.
  66:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c **** 
  67:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****       (#) When a message is received into the CAN Rx FIFOs, it can be retrieved
  68:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****           using the HAL_CAN_GetRxMessage() function. The function
  69:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****           HAL_CAN_GetRxFifoFillLevel() allows to know how many Rx message are
  70:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****           stored in the Rx Fifo.
  71:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c **** 
  72:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****       (#) Calling the HAL_CAN_Stop() function stops the CAN module.
  73:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c **** 
  74:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****       (#) The deinitialization is achieved with HAL_CAN_DeInit() function.
  75:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c **** 
  76:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c **** 
  77:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****       *** Polling mode operation ***
  78:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****       ==============================
  79:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****     [..]
  80:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****       (#) Reception:
  81:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****             (++) Monitor reception of message using HAL_CAN_GetRxFifoFillLevel()
  82:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****                  until at least one message is received.
  83:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****             (++) Then get the message using HAL_CAN_GetRxMessage().
  84:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c **** 
  85:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****       (#) Transmission:
  86:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****             (++) Monitor the Tx mailboxes availability until at least one Tx
ARM GAS  C:\Users\honor\AppData\Local\Temp\ccqm0Nze.s 			page 3


  87:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****                  mailbox is free, using HAL_CAN_GetTxMailboxesFreeLevel().
  88:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****             (++) Then request transmission of a message using
  89:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****                  HAL_CAN_AddTxMessage().
  90:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c **** 
  91:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c **** 
  92:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****       *** Interrupt mode operation ***
  93:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****       ================================
  94:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****     [..]
  95:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****       (#) Notifications are activated using HAL_CAN_ActivateNotification()
  96:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****           function. Then, the process can be controlled through the
  97:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****           available user callbacks: HAL_CAN_xxxCallback(), using same APIs
  98:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****           HAL_CAN_GetRxMessage() and HAL_CAN_AddTxMessage().
  99:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c **** 
 100:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****       (#) Notifications can be deactivated using
 101:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****           HAL_CAN_DeactivateNotification() function.
 102:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c **** 
 103:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****       (#) Special care should be taken for CAN_IT_RX_FIFO0_MSG_PENDING and
 104:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****           CAN_IT_RX_FIFO1_MSG_PENDING notifications. These notifications trig
 105:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****           the callbacks HAL_CAN_RxFIFO0MsgPendingCallback() and
 106:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****           HAL_CAN_RxFIFO1MsgPendingCallback(). User has two possible options
 107:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****           here.
 108:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****             (++) Directly get the Rx message in the callback, using
 109:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****                  HAL_CAN_GetRxMessage().
 110:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****             (++) Or deactivate the notification in the callback without
 111:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****                  getting the Rx message. The Rx message can then be got later
 112:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****                  using HAL_CAN_GetRxMessage(). Once the Rx message have been
 113:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****                  read, the notification can be activated again.
 114:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c **** 
 115:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c **** 
 116:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****       *** Sleep mode ***
 117:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****       ==================
 118:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****     [..]
 119:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****       (#) The CAN peripheral can be put in sleep mode (low power), using
 120:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****           HAL_CAN_RequestSleep(). The sleep mode will be entered as soon as the
 121:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****           current CAN activity (transmission or reception of a CAN frame) will
 122:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****           be completed.
 123:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c **** 
 124:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****       (#) A notification can be activated to be informed when the sleep mode
 125:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****           will be entered.
 126:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c **** 
 127:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****       (#) It can be checked if the sleep mode is entered using
 128:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****           HAL_CAN_IsSleepActive().
 129:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****           Note that the CAN state (accessible from the API HAL_CAN_GetState())
 130:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****           is HAL_CAN_STATE_SLEEP_PENDING as soon as the sleep mode request is
 131:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****           submitted (the sleep mode is not yet entered), and become
 132:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****           HAL_CAN_STATE_SLEEP_ACTIVE when the sleep mode is effective.
 133:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c **** 
 134:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****       (#) The wake-up from sleep mode can be triggered by two ways:
 135:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****             (++) Using HAL_CAN_WakeUp(). When returning from this function,
 136:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****                  the sleep mode is exited (if return status is HAL_OK).
 137:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****             (++) When a start of Rx CAN frame is detected by the CAN peripheral,
 138:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****                  if automatic wake up mode is enabled.
 139:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c **** 
 140:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****   *** Callback registration ***
 141:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****   =============================================
 142:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c **** 
 143:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****   The compilation define  USE_HAL_CAN_REGISTER_CALLBACKS when set to 1
ARM GAS  C:\Users\honor\AppData\Local\Temp\ccqm0Nze.s 			page 4


 144:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****   allows the user to configure dynamically the driver callbacks.
 145:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****   Use Function HAL_CAN_RegisterCallback() to register an interrupt callback.
 146:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c **** 
 147:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****   Function HAL_CAN_RegisterCallback() allows to register following callbacks:
 148:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****     (+) TxMailbox0CompleteCallback   : Tx Mailbox 0 Complete Callback.
 149:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****     (+) TxMailbox1CompleteCallback   : Tx Mailbox 1 Complete Callback.
 150:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****     (+) TxMailbox2CompleteCallback   : Tx Mailbox 2 Complete Callback.
 151:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****     (+) TxMailbox0AbortCallback      : Tx Mailbox 0 Abort Callback.
 152:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****     (+) TxMailbox1AbortCallback      : Tx Mailbox 1 Abort Callback.
 153:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****     (+) TxMailbox2AbortCallback      : Tx Mailbox 2 Abort Callback.
 154:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****     (+) RxFifo0MsgPendingCallback    : Rx Fifo 0 Message Pending Callback.
 155:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****     (+) RxFifo0FullCallback          : Rx Fifo 0 Full Callback.
