 187:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****   By default, after the HAL_CAN_Init() and when the state is HAL_CAN_STATE_RESET,
 188:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****   all callbacks are set to the corresponding weak functions:
 189:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****   example HAL_CAN_ErrorCallback().
 190:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****   Exception done for MspInit and MspDeInit functions that are
 191:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****   reset to the legacy weak function in the HAL_CAN_Init()/ HAL_CAN_DeInit() only when
 192:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****   these callbacks are null (not registered beforehand).
 193:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****   if not, MspInit or MspDeInit are not null, the HAL_CAN_Init()/ HAL_CAN_DeInit()
 194:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****   keep and use the user MspInit/MspDeInit callbacks (registered beforehand)
 195:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c **** 
 196:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****   Callbacks can be registered/unregistered in HAL_CAN_STATE_READY state only.
 197:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****   Exception done MspInit/MspDeInit that can be registered/unregistered
 198:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****   in HAL_CAN_STATE_READY or HAL_CAN_STATE_RESET state,
 199:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****   thus registered (user) MspInit/DeInit callbacks can be used during the Init/DeInit.
 200:frameworks/f407/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_can.c ****   In that case first register the MspInit/MspDeInit user callbacks
